  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a poster, I want to search and browse trending GIFs, as the legacy app allowed, so that this legacy function is not lost.\n\n### Scope\n\nModelled on LOT-056: a `GiphyClient` in HFRNetwork over `HTTPTransport`/URLSession calling Giphy's public REST API (search, trending), rating as legacy (R), typed errors. **No Giphy SDK** (a binary SDK would be a new dependency, AGENTS §3.3). API key and base URL injected as configuration (ADR 0007): a build without a key disables the feature. Search terms are the only user data sent. Tests on REST responses **recorded on the Mac** (key stripped from URLs and bodies), never hand-built. Docs in the same PR: the LOT-071 spec marks T5 'kept' (REST, no SDK, notice N1, data sent = search terms) and HFR-PROTOCOL/third-party notes cite the API shape.\n\n- Module: HFRNetwork · Difficulty: easy · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: legacy parity (no FEAT)\n- Absorbs: Phase 4 backlog 'Giphy (E-10)'; LOT-071 T5 (kept by the operator 2026-10-27, integrated like the Chevereto rehost T4 / LOT-056); ADR 0007\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `HFRswiftApp.swift:9, 20` (SDK configured with an embedded key: not carried over), `AnswerView.swift:533, 2305-2335` (picker, rating R, inserts `[img]<gif URL>[/img]`)\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-098-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-040 (#66, done)\n- LOT-071 (#95, done)\n\n### Blocked by\n\ncapture CAP-N7 (#175) (recorded Giphy search and trending responses) must exist before the decoder is written (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- CAP-N7 (#175): Giphy REST API: one `search` and one `trending` response (rating R), recorded on the Mac with the key stripped from URLs and bodies\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] No third-party SDK and no new package; key and base URL only from configuration (ADR 0007), absent key → feature off (test).\n- [ ] Requests (path, query, rating) and response decoding tested with the mock transport on the CAP-N7 (#175) recordings; no key in any committed fixture (gitleaks green).\n- [ ] LOT-071 spec: T5 row says 'kept: REST API, no SDK, notice N1, search terms only'; the 'undecided' wording is gone.\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-098-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
